{'symbol': 'DGX', 'date': '2021-09-28 07:03:00', 'title': 'OVER HALF OF U.S. CHILDREN HAVE DETECTABLE LEVELS OF LEAD IN THEIR BLOOD, FINDS QUEST DIAGNOSTICS HEALTH TRENDS® STUDY PUBLISHED IN JAMA PEDIATRICS', 'text': 'SECAUCUS, N.J., SEPT. 28, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0ONE IN TWO (50.5%) AMERICAN CHILDREN UNDER SIX YEARS OF AGE TESTED HAVE DETECTABLE LEVELS OF LEAD, A TOXIC METAL, IN THEIR BLOOD, ACCORDING TO A NEW HEALTH TRENDS® STUDY FROM QUEST DIAGNOSTICS (NYSE: DGX) RELEASED TODAY AND PUBLISHED IN JAMA PEDIATRICS.'}